 nths\\nCategory: Arts & Crafts\\n\\nFrom 1976 to 1987 artist Calvin B. Jon
 es along with fellow artist Mitchell Canton painted six murals on the Sout
 h and West sides of Chicago. Jones was active in the Black Arts Movement o
 f the 1960s and 1970s and aesthetically influenced by Chicago's AfriCOBRA 
 collective (African Commune of Bad Relevant Artists)\, known for painting 
 with bold dues they called Cool-Ade colors. Learn more in our archives! Th
 is fun\, hands-on program welcomes families to discover the life and work 
 of Jones while explo\\n\\nMore info: https://chipublib.bibliocommons.com/e
 vents/6a6a43090d65ac3600430ec2
