DESCRIPTION:Organizer: Chicago Public Library\\nCost: free\\nAges: 0-60 mo
 nths\\nCategory: Arts & Crafts\\n\\nJoin four artists from the exhibition 
 to talk about process and decision making in quilting practices. Alejandro
  McGhee\, Amy Basque\, Claire Prucher and Laura Mariela Aranda all approac
 h the craft in different ways\, and their processes have been shaped by th
 e community input at queer quilting workshops. We will look at in-progress
  documentation of the quilts in the show and hear about the series of smal
 l decisions they made to get to the finished artwork. Moderated by curator
  and teacher Eliza Fe\\n\\nMore info: https://chipublib.bibliocommons.com/
